WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.810
The Mourne Mountains.

2
00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.850
The Causeway Coast.

3
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:09.030
Across England, Scotland and Wales,
the UK has 15 National Parks.

4
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.610
The Republic of Ireland had 6 in 2011.

5
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.590
Northern Ireland has none.

6
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.710
A National Park in the Mournes
was proposed back in 2002.

7
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.850
So why does Northern Ireland
still have no National Park?

8
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.150
In this mission, you'll compare
the ways land is protected,

9
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.190
from scientific sites to whole landscapes.

10
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.210
Then you'll follow the Mournes proposal,
and weigh the arguments on both sides.

11
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.450
Your mission: find out why Northern
Ireland still lacks a National Park,

12
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.670
and judge whether it should have one.
